# TOTP tests made deterministic (2026-11-14). TEST-BUG RE-LOCK, append-only: the previous hashes of these files stay valid history.
# Reason: tests/unit/backend-merit-reviewer.test.js RV6 failed once in CI (run 43464554484) with 400 "invalid TOTP code". The test makes a
# code with Date.now() (step - 1, so that a later code of the current step is not a replay) and the Worker verifies it with its own Date.now();
# when the wall clock crosses a 30 s step boundary between the two, step - 1 falls outside the Worker's window (previous / current / next step).
# Reproduced deterministically by running the unchanged file with Date.now() read 31 s later inside backend/src (RV2-RV8 fail), and gone after the fix.
# Fix: tests/unit/totp-clock.js freezes the shared clock (node:test mock.timers, Date only) 10 s into a 30 s step for the whole file, so the generator
# and the Worker see the same instant. One added require line per file; NO assertion, fixture or expectation was changed, removed or weakened.
# Files that generate TOTP codes from Date.now(): all ten are frozen the same way (the others only use the current step, but two codes "of the current
# step" can also straddle a boundary and defeat a replay assertion).
# 20 consecutive runs of the ten files together: 20 of 20 green (132 tests each).
